# Quest! hard rules

Current plan: `docs/design/ULTRA-PLAN-2026-11-20.md`. Task cards: `docs/design/CURSOR-HANDOFF-2026-11-20.md`. Active build: `docs/design/CURSOR-BUILD-2-2026-11-20.md` (after the big build finishes).

- **No hosted services.** Never run `supabase db push`, Supabase MCP/plugin SQL, edge function deploys, Vercel deploys, or EAS build/submit/update. The owner does these.
- **Git.** Never push to `main`, force-push, merge or close PRs. Work on your own `cursor/<card>-<name>` branch. Integration-branch exception: you may `git merge --no-ff` your own card branches into the integration branch of the active build plan (`cursor/big-build`, then `cursor/build-2`) and push that branch. Never merge into `main` or the base branch.
- **Migrations.** Never edit or rename the baseline or 002–040: they are applied in production. 041–045 are not applied yet. Build 2 may fix them in place, but only while the matching `docs/design/OWNER-RUNSHEET.md` row is unticked and the owner hasn't said it was applied. Otherwise write a new `046+` migration. Reserved: 044 stickers, 045 duo quests.
- **No SQL against the hosted project, ever.** SQL runs only in CI's throwaway local Supabase stack (build 2, `scripts/db-local/*`), or locally if Docker is running.
- New `completions`/`profiles` columns need an explicit `GRANT SELECT (col)` to anon/authenticated (038/039 removed table SELECT).
- SECURITY DEFINER functions: `SET search_path` and `REVOKE` from PUBLIC/anon/authenticated unless clients call them.
- XP, streaks, stickers and verification are server-authoritative. The client never computes or writes them.
- `lib/submitCompletion.ts` is the only upload → insert → reward path. The submit screen enqueues only on a `network` result.
- Analytics events carry no coordinates, photos, usernames or free text. UI never says "verified" before the server accepts.
- Every admin server action calls `requireAdmin()`.
- Mobile UI: `lib/theme.ts` tokens only (no hex/rgb/raw fontSize), Figtree, sentence case, no emoji, 48pt targets, skeletons not spinners, stickers not sprites (`docs/design/BRAND.md`).
- App tests are plain Node scripts; no new JS test frameworks. Build 2 adds pgTAP (`supabase test db`) for SQL and `deno test` for edge functions, nothing else. Run the geofence and mobile tests and `tsc` (plus admin `tsc` and `next build` if admin changed) before reporting.
- Stay inside your card's file list (ultra plan §4). If you need another file, stop and report.
